Dawamu OS - KCSE Set Book Study Guide
TITLE: Fathers of Nations
AUTHOR: Paul B. Vitta
GENRE: Compulsory KCSE English Literature Novel

SYNOPSIS:
The novel depicts a pan-African summit at the luxurious Pinnacle Hotel in Banjul, The Gambia. African heads of state meet to debate "Way Omega", a development paradigm sponsored by foreign powers. Four disenfranchised Africans (Prof. Kimani from Kenya, Pastor Chiamaka from Nigeria, Comrade Melusi from Zimbabwe, and Engineer Tahir from Libya) are organized by AGDA to champion "Path Alpha", emphasizing integrity, local empowerment, and authentic African self-governance.

KEY CHARACTERS:
1. Professor Karanja Kimani: Economics lecturer who lost his daughter in a car crash and whose wife abandoned him for a corrupt MP.
2. Pastor Chineke Chiamaka: Former fiery Lagos preacher jailed for condemning military dictatorship.
3. Comrade Melusi: Liberation struggle war hero sidelined into poverty by the post-colonial regime.
4. Engineer Seif Tahir: Nuclear scientist whose life's work was scrapped due to foreign geopolitical pressure.
5. Dr. Abiola Afolabi: Elite advisor secretly acting as the "Guide" orchestrating Path Alpha.
6. Fiona McKenzie: Inquisitive journalist exposing high-level corruption.

MAJOR THEMES:
- Dictatorship, Corruption, and Impunity in Post-Independence Africa.
- Betrayal and Disillusionment of the Common Citizen.
- Neo-Colonialism and Donor Dependence.
- Hope, Youth, and Pan-African Redemption.

